<%- include('partials/header') %>
    <div class="page">
        <section>
            <div>
                <h1>How to Host</h1>
                <p>Hosting a Gender Reveal Bingo Party is relatively cheap and fairly straight-forward.</p>
                <p>These instructions will explain everything you need to know to have the best experience with your gender reveal.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="about-games">
            <div>
                <h2>About Games</h2>
                <p>Before you can play Gender Reveal Bingo Party, you'll need to purchase a game.</p>
                <p>Games can be purchased via the button below.</p>
                <div class="purchase-div">
                    <a href="/purchase-game/checkout" class="button">Purchase a Game</a>
                    <p><%- price %> + tax</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div>
                <p>After purchasing a game, the game will appear in your account.</p>
                <img draggable="false" src="images/demo/new-game.png"/>
            </div>

            <div>
                <p>Once you have a game, you'll want to explore the "About Game" page.</p>
                <img draggable="false" src="images/demo/about-game.png" />
                <p>This button allows you to view and edit your game in the following ways:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Set the gender and title of the game</li>
                    <li>Create an edit link<br>(edit links allow doctors or friends to set the gender of your game without accessing your account)</li>
                    <li>Download a copy of the winning card<br>(if the game has been played)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="about-cards">
            <div>
                <h2>About Cards</h2>
                <p>Our game player only works with our unique cards.</p>
                <%- include('svgs/fanned-cards') %>
                <p>Before launching a game, you'll want to consider how your guests will access their bingo cards.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div>
                <p>Guests can access a digital bingo card through their phone or use a paper copy.</p>
                <img draggable="false" src="images/demo/card-types.png" />
                <caption>Image created with Google Gemini</caption>
                <p>Our game player does not require all players to use paper cards or digital cards exclusively.</p>
                <p>As the host, you can decide whether your group will use paper cards, digital cards, or a mix of both.</p>
                <p>Specific info about each card type is listed below.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <h3>Paper Cards</h3>
                <p>If paper cards will be used, they will need to be printed and cut beforehand.</p>
                <p>Download the print file for free!</p>
                <a class="button" href="downloads/gender-reveal-bingo-cards.pdf" download>Download PDF</a>
            </div>
            
            <div>
                <h3>Digital Cards</h3>
                <p>If digital cards will be used, it's important to know how your guests will access them.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <p>During a live game, on the card registration page, press the "Show QR Code" button.</p>
                <img draggable="false" src="images/demo/show-qr.png" />
            </div>

            <div>
                <p>This will pull up a QR code that can be used to access a digital bingo card.</p>
                <img draggable="false" src="images/qr-bingo-card.svg" style="max-height: 350px; box-shadow: none;"/>
                <p>If anyone has trouble scanning the QR code, they can manually type the link at the bottom of the QR code.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <p>The link will take them to the following page:</p>
                <img draggable="false" src="images/demo/playable-card.png"/>
                <p>*Please Note*</p>
                <p>Players won't be able to access a digital card until they are given an ID by the host.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <p>When a player needs to register a digital bingo card, follow the process below:</p>
            </div>

            <%- include('partials/registering-digital-cards') %>
        </section>

        <section id="playing-the-game">
            <div>
                <h2>Playing the Game</h2>
                <p>Once you've configured your game, and have prepared the bingo cards (if applicable), you'll be ready to launch the game!</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="add-to-home-screen">
            <div>
                <h2>Add to Home Screen</h2>
                <p>Some browsers (usually smart phones) disable the fullscreen feature.  This can make our game player look clunky or crowded.</p>
                <p>For the best experience, we recommend adding our site to your home screen (to allow the fullscreen feature).</p>
            </div>
            
            <div>
                <p>For Safari:</p>
                <p>Open the website in Safari.</p>
                <p>Tap the Share button at the bottom (the square with the arrow pointing up: 📤).</p>
                <p>Scroll down and tap "Add to Home Screen".</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <p>On Android (Chrome):</p>
                <p>Open the website in Chrome.</p>
                <p>Tap the three dots in the top right corner (⋮).</p>
                <p>Tap Add to Home screen (or Install app).</p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <p>If problems persist:</p>
                <p>Ask Gemini or ChatGPT something like "How do I add a site to my home screen with my specific browser?"</p>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>